WEBVTT

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.951
Alert! Alert!

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.254
Decompression on Platform 684!

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.294
Brace for hull rupture!

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.158
Thrusters are down!

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.027
We're going to crash!

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.333
Hey, what do you think?

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.962
Look at the detail
on that dorsal plating.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.469
Impressive.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.769
Are you sure you're
willing to part with it?

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.071
I just hope your boy enjoys it
as much as I do.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.406
I'm certain he will

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:48.174
if we make it home
in time for his birthday.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.237
We'll make it.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.512
If you and Sivad
had a child of your own,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.076
you'd have an excuse
to play with toys more often.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.851
I'm detecting a fluctuation
in tank 4.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.087
There's a full-scale rupture
in progress!

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.424
Isolate the deck.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:06.488
Activate the emergency
containment field.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.433
The emergency systems
are off-line.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.902
Backup controls are down, too.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:12.938
Eject the tank.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.940
Here?!
There's an inhabited sys...

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.440
We have no choice.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.309
The ejection ports
aren't responding.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.370
Impossible.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.984
There's another rupture forming
in tank 6.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.883
We'll have to send
somebody down there

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.424
to seal off
the tanks manually.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.050
Contact the Theta Corps.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.719
Communications are down.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.331
Get down to the injector pod
and seal those tanks.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.460
I didn't sign up
for core labor.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.730
I'm giving you an order.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.533
I'll be contaminated.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.039
Now!

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:53.291
The flame, like emotion,
is a primitive force.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:57.735
Left unchecked,
it's chaotic, destructive,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:04:01.331
but, if controlled,
it can be a powerful tool.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:04.672
The lamp controls the flame,
as you must learn

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.904
to control your emotions.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.605
I lost my temper...
no big deal.

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:12.276
You destroyed the Doctor's
holographic camera.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:16.049
I told him three times
to leave Engineering,

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.714
but he kept buzzing around

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.190
snapping pictures
for some photo essay.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.558
"A day in the life
of the warp core."

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:26.656
I apologized, and I replicated
him a new camera.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:30.294
You have a long history
of emotional volatility.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.338
The point of this exercise

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:35.067
is not to atone
for past transgressions,

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:37.234
but to prevent future ones.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.710
You can't order
someone to meditate.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:43.476
Commander Chakotay
thinks otherwise.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.522
Are my eyes supposed to be open
or closed for this part?

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:59.429
Whichever allows you
to focus your mind.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.767
Envision the flame
burning within you.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.238
Sorry.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:13.575
The flame grows hotter...

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.910
a point of white light.

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:18.677
Follow it backward
through the years

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:21.345
to a time when you were
younger, a child.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.790
Is there something amusing,
Lieutenant?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:31.390
I'm sorry. An image
just flashed through my mind.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.227
You as a child.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.392
Those pointy little ears.

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.595
You must have been cute.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.365
Indeed.

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:41.930
Please follow my instructions

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:44.238
or we'll discontinue
this exercise.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.443
Right.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.444
Me... childhood.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.445
How old?

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:49.811
Your earliest memories.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.747
Try to recall a time

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:54.343
when you experienced
uncontrollable anger.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.153
Daniel Bird.

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.626
I beg your pardon?

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.460
Well, he was one

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.125
of my classmates
in grammar school.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:10.396
He was always terrorizing me.

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:15.097
He used to point
at my cranial ridges

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:18.507
and tease me
about being half-Klingon.

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:20.739
He called me...

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.474
"Miss Turtlehead."

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.812
That angered you.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.249
Of course, it did.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:31.282
So I attacked him once,
during recess...

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:32.790
on the gyro-swing.

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:35.054
I disengaged
the centrifugal governor.

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:37.460
He was spinning so fast,
he almost flew apart.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.589
Then I yanked him off the swing

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.633
and started pounding
his little face.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.602
If Miss Malvin hadn't showed up,
I probably would have...

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.467
Describe the anger
you felt at that moment.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.369
I...

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.603
I wanted to hurt him.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:57.308
To take revenge for all
the humiliation he caused me.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:00.944
Your anger was
a source of strength.

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:04.545
It protected you,
gave you courage.

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:08.617
I suppose it did.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.787
And, when the Doctor
tried to take

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.194
a holo-photograph of you?

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:13.527
I was annoyed.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.567
He kept getting in the way.

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:18.263
The rage within you runs deep.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:21.170
It's been with you
for many years.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.800
I'm not a Vulcan.
I'll survive.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:26.677
Whatever you say...

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:28.043
Miss Turtlehead.

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:30.082
What did you say?

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:32.049
You're easily provoked.

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:35.178
You must learn
to master your emotions.

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.722
I've had enough mastery
for one day.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.655
School's out.

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:54.696
So, how'd it go
with B'Elanna today?

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:57.572
Our meditation sessions
are confidential.

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:00.271
No. I'm not asking
for sordid details.

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:03.873
I just want to know
if you think you can help her.

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:07.350
Her training will be
a challenge for both of us.

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:10.855
Take it from me,
getting B'Elanna

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.982
to control her temper
is like convincing

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:15.220
a Ferengi to leave
his estate to charity.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:19.159
Captain, we're receiving
an automated distress call.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.426
Origin.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.229
Coordinates 121 by 268.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:24.633
Range: Two billion kilometers.

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:26.035
Who's sending it?

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:27.732
I can't tell.

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:29.672
Let them know help's on the way.
Set a course, Mr. Paris.

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:45.887
37 escape pods.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:49.121
They're contaminated
with theta radiation.

00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:50.127
Malon?

00:08:50.196 --> 00:08:51.720
Possibly. Life signs?

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:53.924
Two, but they're erratic.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.194
Beam them to Sick Bay.

00:08:55.268 --> 00:08:57.498
Initiate biohazard
containment procedures.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.435
Theta radiation has affected

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.439
a radius
of 600 million kilometers.

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:02.838
Source?

00:09:02.909 --> 00:09:05.639
A Malon freighter traveling
at high impulse.

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:07.576
It appears to be abandoned.

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:12.215
I thought we'd seen
the last of the Malon.

00:09:12.285 --> 00:09:14.378
I guess they're looking
for new places

00:09:14.453 --> 00:09:15.977
to dump their toxic waste.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.886
Do we know what happened
to their ship?

00:09:17.957 --> 00:09:18.889
Were they attacked?

00:09:19.025 --> 00:09:20.515
I'm just as curious as you are.

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:22.026
Can you revive either of them?

00:09:29.502 --> 00:09:31.333
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:09:31.404 --> 00:09:33.338
Fesek...

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:37.699
Controller Fesek.

00:09:37.777 --> 00:09:39.301
Where am I?

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:40.310
You're on my vessel.

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:41.903
We responded
to your distress call.

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:42.912
My ship...

00:09:43.049 --> 00:09:44.277
It's heavily damaged.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:45.282
Where?

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:46.784
Three million kilometers
from here.

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:49.013
That's too close;
we've got to get further away.

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:52.023
Calm down. Calm down.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:54.082
Tell me what's wrong
with your ship.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.149
Why did you abandon it?

00:09:58.965 --> 00:10:01.729
We were
on a waste export mission.

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:03.291
Dumping theta radiation.

00:10:03.369 --> 00:10:05.929
Two of the theta tanks ruptured.

00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:08.768
Systems malfunctioned
one-by-one...

00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:12.277
communications, navigation,
propulsion.

00:10:12.345 --> 00:10:14.609
We had no choice.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.944
Radiation was venting
from every port.

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:21.076
Over 60 crewmen died
within minutes.

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.347
It was chaos.

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:26.380
We stumbled through the gas
to get to the escape pods.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:28.427
Only a few of us made it.

00:10:32.598 --> 00:10:35.396
Where are the others?

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:38.699
The two of you were
the only ones we found alive.

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:51.048
Listen to me... very carefully.

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:54.415
The fact that we're still here

00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:56.978
means the ship hasn't
exploded... yet.

00:10:57.056 --> 00:11:00.992
When it does, over four trillion
isotons of antimatter waste

00:11:01.127 --> 00:11:03.152
is going to ignite.

00:11:03.229 --> 00:11:06.892
Everything within three
light-years will be destroyed.

00:11:07.967 --> 00:11:09.525
Janeway to the Bridge.

00:11:09.602 --> 00:11:10.534
Go ahead.

00:11:10.603 --> 00:11:11.934
Put at least five light-years
between us

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:13.130
and the Malon freighter,
quickly.

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:14.467
You heard her, Tom.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.371
Send out a sector-wide alert.

00:11:16.442 --> 00:11:18.637
Warn any other ships
in the vicinity

00:11:18.711 --> 00:11:20.611
to evacuate immediately.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.375
Our warp field just collapsed.

00:11:22.448 --> 00:11:25.417
All this theta radiation,
it's disrupting subspace.

00:11:25.484 --> 00:11:27.816
Can you reinitialize the field?

00:11:27.887 --> 00:11:28.979
Negative.

00:11:30.289 --> 00:11:31.881
Tuvok...

00:11:31.957 --> 00:11:33.185
Without warp drive,

00:11:33.259 --> 00:11:35.420
there's no chance
we'll clear the blast radius.

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:36.756
Agreed.

00:11:36.829 --> 00:11:39.263
Mr. Paris, set a course
for the freighter, full impulse.

00:11:39.331 --> 00:11:41.265
- Aye, Captain.
- What?!

00:11:41.333 --> 00:11:43.893
If we can't outrun your ship,
maybe we can disable it.

00:11:43.969 --> 00:11:45.493
Every deck has been
contaminated.

00:11:45.571 --> 00:11:48.165
Anyone who goes on board
will liquefy within minutes.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.832
We'll find a way.

00:11:49.909 --> 00:11:53.106
We? I'm not going
anywhere near that vessel.

00:11:53.179 --> 00:11:55.374
You can either stay and help us

00:11:55.448 --> 00:11:57.609
or I'll send you back
to your escape pod.

00:11:57.683 --> 00:11:58.650
Your choice.

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:01.843
Clean them up, Doctor.

00:12:01.921 --> 00:12:03.752
I need them on the Bridge.

00:12:21.273 --> 00:12:24.333
How long until those
storage tanks explode?

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.344
Approximately six hours.

00:12:26.412 --> 00:12:28.073
Can we get
an away team on board?

00:12:28.147 --> 00:12:29.739
The freighter's hull is intact.

00:12:29.815 --> 00:12:31.840
Life support appears
to be operational.

00:12:31.917 --> 00:12:33.145
However, 33 of 42 decks

00:12:33.219 --> 00:12:35.687
are flooded with high levels
of theta radiation.

00:12:35.755 --> 00:12:37.120
Including the control room,

00:12:37.189 --> 00:12:39.589
which is where we'd have to go
to reestablish containment.

00:12:39.658 --> 00:12:40.625
As I told you...

00:12:40.693 --> 00:12:42.456
We could beam onto one
of the lower levels

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:43.825
where there's less radiation

00:12:43.896 --> 00:12:45.955
and vent the contaminated
sections one by one.

00:12:46.065 --> 00:12:47.794
Clear a path
to the control room.

00:12:47.867 --> 00:12:49.960
I appreciate
what you're trying to do,

00:12:50.069 --> 00:12:52.629
but, if what you're
considering were possible,

00:12:52.705 --> 00:12:55.503
we'd have tried it before
we abandoned the ship.

00:12:55.574 --> 00:12:57.166
We have years of experience

00:12:57.243 --> 00:12:58.767
aboard freighters
of this gradient.

00:12:58.844 --> 00:12:59.970
Your experience

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:02.239
is what got us into this
mess in the first place.

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:04.248
That's enough, Lieutenant.

00:13:04.316 --> 00:13:05.908
Maybe there's another way.

00:13:06.051 --> 00:13:07.177
I'm listening.

00:13:07.253 --> 00:13:08.914
Four hours from here,

00:13:08.988 --> 00:13:11.422
there's a nebula
that could protect us

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.422
from the blast.

00:13:12.491 --> 00:13:13.856
We could alter course...

00:13:13.926 --> 00:13:16.224
wait there
until after the explosion.

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:19.196
There are at least three
other ships in the sector.

00:13:19.265 --> 00:13:20.527
What about them?

00:13:20.599 --> 00:13:22.692
I don't see what we can do.

00:13:22.768 --> 00:13:24.929
So hundreds of people
become contaminated

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:27.698
because you're not willing
to clean up your garbage.

00:13:27.773 --> 00:13:29.570
Lieutenant.

00:13:29.642 --> 00:13:30.904
Assemble an away team.

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:32.534
We're going over there.

00:13:32.611 --> 00:13:33.339
Wait!

00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:37.377
Tell them about the vihaar.

00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:39.314
What's he talking about?

00:13:39.385 --> 00:13:40.943
Nothing. It's a myth.

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:43.213
What kind of myth?

00:13:43.289 --> 00:13:47.248
It's an old story
shared among freighter crews.

00:13:47.326 --> 00:13:50.955
Some of them say
they've seen creatures

00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:52.586
in the theta storage tanks.

00:13:52.665 --> 00:13:54.599
Creatures?

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:56.498
Created by radiogenic wastes.

00:13:56.569 --> 00:14:00.562
According to the legend,
they are poisonous monsters

00:14:00.639 --> 00:14:03.107
that wreak havoc
aboard Malon ships.

00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:05.541
It's a common belief

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:07.772
among our more
superstitious recruits.

00:14:07.847 --> 00:14:10.475
I never believed it myself,
but during the evacuation,

00:14:10.549 --> 00:14:12.915
some of the crew people
saw something, a form.

00:14:12.985 --> 00:14:15.419
Hallucinations are one
of the first symptoms

00:14:15.487 --> 00:14:16.454
of theta poisoning.

00:14:16.522 --> 00:14:17.682
You know that.

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:20.247
Maybe. Then how do you
explain what happened?

00:14:20.326 --> 00:14:21.691
We checked every system.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:22.818
You'd say anything

00:14:22.895 --> 00:14:25.386
to get out of going back
to that freighter.

00:14:25.464 --> 00:14:27.022
If you'd been there...

00:14:27.099 --> 00:14:29.761
you'd be afraid to go back, too.

00:14:32.238 --> 00:14:32.338
This chamber seems to be
the least affected by radiation.

00:14:32.338 --> 00:14:35.034
This chamber seems to be
the least affected by radiation.

00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:36.404
We'll beam in there.

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:38.466
That's 15 decks
below the control room.

00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:40.944
We'll have to work our way up.

00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:43.914
The pressurization systems,
they're off-line.

00:14:43.983 --> 00:14:45.348
How will we vent the gas?

00:14:45.417 --> 00:14:47.851
There are two main
air locks on each deck.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.319
We'll open them as we go...

00:14:49.388 --> 00:14:51.686
perform a series
of controlled decompressions.

00:14:51.757 --> 00:14:53.622
What's to stop us
from being vented?

00:14:53.692 --> 00:14:55.057
Force fields.

00:14:55.127 --> 00:14:57.823
I spent six years aboard
a Talaxian garbage scow.

00:14:57.897 --> 00:15:00.331
I know a few things
about waste management.

00:15:00.399 --> 00:15:03.596
Even low levels of theta
radiation can be lethal.

00:15:03.669 --> 00:15:05.569
Our Doctor's developed
an inoculation.

00:15:05.638 --> 00:15:07.469
It'll temporarily
prevent our cells

00:15:07.539 --> 00:15:09.063
from absorbing the radiation.

00:15:09.141 --> 00:15:10.403
How long will it last?

00:15:10.476 --> 00:15:11.704
Two, three hours.

00:15:11.777 --> 00:15:13.244
Half of the doors
and bulkheads are fused.

00:15:13.312 --> 00:15:14.244
The ascenders are off-line.

00:15:14.313 --> 00:15:15.610
It could take us
twice as long as that

00:15:15.681 --> 00:15:16.613
to reach the control room.

00:15:16.682 --> 00:15:17.910
Then we'll have to work quickly.

00:15:17.983 --> 00:15:20.508
We'll take phasers
to cut through any obstacles.

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:23.316
I've ordered my men to do
a lot of risky things,

00:15:23.389 --> 00:15:25.653
but nothing as foolish as this.

00:15:25.724 --> 00:15:27.191
More foolish than towing around

00:15:27.259 --> 00:15:29.727
a trillion isotons
of toxic waste?

00:15:29.795 --> 00:15:32.059
We take every precaution
to keep it contained.

00:15:32.131 --> 00:15:34.031
Until you dump it
in someone's backyard.

00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:36.795
Is your crew always
so... diplomatic?

00:15:36.869 --> 00:15:38.427
Your concerns are noted.

00:15:38.504 --> 00:15:39.732
Get them inoculated.

00:15:39.805 --> 00:15:42.273
We'll meet you
in Transporter Room 1.

00:15:45.377 --> 00:15:49.245
We're trying to avoid
explosions, remember?

00:15:49.315 --> 00:15:51.180
Oh, not another lecture
about my emotions.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.081
No. A lecture
about how to treat guests

00:15:53.152 --> 00:15:54.517
aboard this ship.

00:15:54.586 --> 00:15:57.419
Guests? Chakotay, these people
are the scourge of the Quadrant.

00:15:57.489 --> 00:15:58.820
Agreed. But right now,

00:15:58.891 --> 00:16:01.223
they're our only hope
of repairing that freighter,

00:16:01.293 --> 00:16:03.727
so I suggest you make friends.

00:16:03.796 --> 00:16:05.525
Diplomacy...

00:16:05.597 --> 00:16:07.861
Janeway's answer to everything.

00:16:07.933 --> 00:16:09.491
This isn't the Captain talking.

00:16:09.568 --> 00:16:11.399
It's me,
and I'm giving you an order.

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:12.767
Keep your temper in check.

00:16:12.838 --> 00:16:13.862
Understood?

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.207
Understood?

00:16:16.275 --> 00:16:17.242
Yeah.

00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:18.571
I didn't hear you.

00:16:18.644 --> 00:16:19.611
Yes.

00:16:19.678 --> 00:16:22.374
B'Elanna, I need your expertise
on this mission,

00:16:22.448 --> 00:16:23.745
not your bad mood.

00:16:24.984 --> 00:16:26.451
I'll see what I can do.

00:16:50.142 --> 00:16:51.575
Ready, Neelix?

00:16:51.643 --> 00:16:52.803
Uh, not quite.

00:16:52.878 --> 00:16:54.311
Do we still have a minute?

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.144
It's just... it's
not quite strong enough yet.

00:16:57.216 --> 00:16:59.343
Oh...

00:16:59.418 --> 00:17:02.319
Would you mind passing me
that little dish?

00:17:02.388 --> 00:17:04.720
Neelix, I admire
your dedication,

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.384
but the crew can figure
out lunch on their own.

00:17:07.459 --> 00:17:09.859
Lunch and dinner
and a midnight snack

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:11.793
have all been taken care of.

00:17:11.864 --> 00:17:13.263
This is for me.

00:17:13.332 --> 00:17:16.824
It's a Talaxian
theta radiation remedy...

00:17:16.902 --> 00:17:20.201
crushed Rama leaf
and Katyllian clove.

00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:22.900
It helps fortify
the cellular membranes.

00:17:22.975 --> 00:17:25.273
I think the Doctor's
inoculation might be

00:17:25.344 --> 00:17:26.675
a better way to go.

00:17:26.745 --> 00:17:28.406
Every little bit helps.

00:17:29.848 --> 00:17:31.440
Oh, uh, by the way...

00:17:31.517 --> 00:17:32.916
thank you.

00:17:33.052 --> 00:17:34.178
For what?

00:17:34.253 --> 00:17:36.687
For sending me on such
an important mission...

00:17:36.755 --> 00:17:38.689
not that my duties
in the Mess Hall

00:17:38.757 --> 00:17:39.689
aren't challenging.

00:17:39.758 --> 00:17:40.782
It was an easy choice.

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:42.486
You were the best man
for the job.

00:17:42.561 --> 00:17:45.553
Well... our scow once ran

00:17:45.631 --> 00:17:47.394
smack into a theta
radiation field...

00:17:47.466 --> 00:17:49.127
knocked the propulsion out.

00:17:49.201 --> 00:17:51.499
We had no choice
but to sit there.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:54.095
We were barely alive
when they found us.

00:17:54.173 --> 00:17:57.973
If it hadn't been for this,
nobody would have survived.

00:18:10.289 --> 00:18:13.588
Once you get past the...
the choking reflex...

00:18:13.659 --> 00:18:15.718
it's really not...
really not so bad.

00:18:15.794 --> 00:18:17.056
Want to try some?

00:18:17.129 --> 00:18:18.756
No. I'll take my chances.

00:18:18.831 --> 00:18:21.095
Transporter Room 1
to Commander Chakotay.

00:18:21.166 --> 00:18:22.497
We're ready to proceed.

00:18:22.568 --> 00:18:23.933
On our way.

00:18:27.673 --> 00:18:29.334
B'Elanna...

00:18:29.408 --> 00:18:31.239
aren't you forgetting something?

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:32.709
I don't think so.

00:18:32.778 --> 00:18:35.508
Well... uh, a "good-bye"
would be nice

00:18:35.581 --> 00:18:38.675
"so long," "see you soon"...
something along those lines.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.047
I didn't want to risk it.

00:18:40.119 --> 00:18:41.086
Risk what?

00:18:41.153 --> 00:18:42.347
Starting an argument.

00:18:42.421 --> 00:18:43.479
Ha! Argument? Us?

00:18:43.555 --> 00:18:46.217
So, I hear it's been
a short fuse kind of day.

00:18:46.291 --> 00:18:47.280
About this long.

00:18:47.359 --> 00:18:49.020
Nothing you can't handle.

00:18:49.094 --> 00:18:50.425
If you think so.

00:18:50.496 --> 00:18:51.588
I know so.

00:18:52.998 --> 00:18:55.432
I suppose it's always
going to be like this.

00:18:55.501 --> 00:18:56.433
Like what?

00:18:56.502 --> 00:18:57.935
Me against the galaxy.

00:18:58.003 --> 00:19:00.130
Well, the galaxy
doesn't stand a chance.

00:19:00.205 --> 00:19:01.331
Now... promise me

00:19:01.406 --> 00:19:03.840
that you're going to be
careful over there.

00:19:03.909 --> 00:19:05.206
No stopping to have fun.

00:19:05.277 --> 00:19:08.007
Fun? On a Malon freighter?

00:19:10.449 --> 00:19:11.916
I'll see you soon.

00:19:26.565 --> 00:19:28.692
Well, it's nothing
a fresh coat of paint

00:19:28.767 --> 00:19:29.893
wouldn't brighten up.

00:19:30.002 --> 00:19:31.594
This way.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:36.334
Theta radiation density...
20 million EV per cubic meter.

00:19:36.408 --> 00:19:38.035
Structural integrity is holding.

00:19:39.678 --> 00:19:42.078
I wish I could say the same
for my lungs.

00:19:43.982 --> 00:19:45.472
What was that?

00:19:45.551 --> 00:19:48.247
This corridor's filled
with methogenic particles,

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:49.514
highly charged.

00:19:50.856 --> 00:19:53.825
Something's causing
an electrostatic cascade.

00:19:55.127 --> 00:19:57.823
Our scanning signals
are igniting the particles.

00:19:57.896 --> 00:19:59.090
It's the tricorders.

00:19:59.164 --> 00:20:00.131
Take cover!

00:20:08.774 --> 00:20:10.401
No more tricorders.

00:20:16.815 --> 00:20:18.476
Control mechanisms are down.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.314
We're going to have to open
the air locks manually.

00:20:21.386 --> 00:20:23.251
Wait here.
We'll take care of it.

00:20:23.322 --> 00:20:24.584
B'Elanna, go with them.

00:20:24.656 --> 00:20:26.954
We can do this ourselves.

00:20:27.092 --> 00:20:29.083
I'd prefer to keep an eye
on your progress.

00:20:29.161 --> 00:20:30.492
You're on my freighter.

00:20:30.562 --> 00:20:31.859
I'm in charge here.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:33.397
You abandoned ship, remember?

00:20:33.465 --> 00:20:34.955
You take your orders from me.

00:20:36.235 --> 00:20:38.863
We'll have to crawl
into an injector port.

00:20:38.937 --> 00:20:41.701
It's only big enough
for two people.

00:20:41.773 --> 00:20:43.866
Pelk, you stay with us.

00:20:46.211 --> 00:20:47.508
Shall we?

00:20:57.422 --> 00:21:00.448
How can you stand
to work in these conditions?

00:21:00.525 --> 00:21:02.516
You think we're animals,
don't you?

00:21:02.594 --> 00:21:04.152
You said it, not me.

00:21:04.229 --> 00:21:06.925
I'm a waste controller
half the year.

00:21:07.032 --> 00:21:09.466
Do you know what I do
the rest of the time?

00:21:11.003 --> 00:21:12.595
I'm a sculptor.

00:21:12.671 --> 00:21:13.933
What's your point?

00:21:14.006 --> 00:21:16.566
Every year,
I give up work I love

00:21:16.642 --> 00:21:18.906
to expose myself to radiation

00:21:18.977 --> 00:21:21.445
that will probably
cut my life in half.

00:21:21.513 --> 00:21:22.946
Then why do it?

00:21:23.048 --> 00:21:25.141
Have you ever been
to Malon Prime?

00:21:25.217 --> 00:21:26.912
It's a remarkable place.

00:21:26.985 --> 00:21:30.421
It's one of the most beautiful
worlds you'll ever see.

00:21:30.489 --> 00:21:34.118
Our planet would choke
with industrial wastes

00:21:34.192 --> 00:21:37.252
if it weren't for the sacrifices
of people like me.

00:21:37.329 --> 00:21:39.957
How many worlds are you
willing to contaminate

00:21:40.098 --> 00:21:42.362
to keep your own home so tidy?

00:21:42.434 --> 00:21:44.959
Do you have any idea
of the trouble we go to

00:21:45.037 --> 00:21:48.131
to locate isolated areas?

00:21:55.314 --> 00:21:57.339
Manual actuators.

00:21:57.416 --> 00:21:59.384
I'll release them.

00:21:59.451 --> 00:22:01.612
You monitor
the pressure variance.

00:22:01.687 --> 00:22:03.678
Right.

00:22:05.524 --> 00:22:07.924
Do you have any children?

00:22:07.993 --> 00:22:09.290
No.

00:22:09.361 --> 00:22:11.056
I have a son.

00:22:11.129 --> 00:22:13.324
He's seven years old.

00:22:13.398 --> 00:22:16.925
He wants to be a waste
controller when he grows up.

00:22:17.069 --> 00:22:19.128
You must be very proud.

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:22.937
Ready.

00:22:24.109 --> 00:22:25.406
Torres to Chakotay.

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:28.071
Stand by
for the decompression sequence.

00:22:28.146 --> 00:22:29.340
Acknowledged.

00:22:42.761 --> 00:22:44.319
It didn't work.

00:22:44.396 --> 00:22:48.332
There's something jamming
the air-lock controls.

00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:49.560
Torres to Chakotay.

00:22:49.634 --> 00:22:50.965
We've got a problem.

00:22:51.036 --> 00:22:52.526
The actuators aren't working.

00:22:52.604 --> 00:22:55.937
Somebody's going to have
to go up there and take a look.

00:22:56.007 --> 00:22:58.202
Wait, that deck
is still contaminated.

00:22:58.276 --> 00:22:59.709
I'll go.

00:22:59.778 --> 00:23:02.611
I've been exposed to worse.

00:23:02.681 --> 00:23:03.943
Wait.

00:23:07.419 --> 00:23:09.284
One for the road.

00:23:09.354 --> 00:23:11.754
It's probably
just the decouplers.

00:23:11.823 --> 00:23:14.553
They're always getting
encrusted with oxides.

00:23:36.047 --> 00:23:37.674
Who's there?!

00:24:08.313 --> 00:24:09.678
I... I saw it...

00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:11.716
I saw it...

00:24:11.783 --> 00:24:12.841
What?

00:24:12.918 --> 00:24:14.408
The creature.

00:24:19.157 --> 00:24:21.625
Give me 20 cc's of anesthezine.

00:24:24.863 --> 00:24:26.194
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:24:26.264 --> 00:24:27.526
Transporter status.

00:24:27.599 --> 00:24:29.328
Still too much interference.

00:24:29.401 --> 00:24:31.596
I'll try compensating. Stand by
for further instructions.

00:24:31.670 --> 00:24:32.796
What happened?

00:24:32.871 --> 00:24:33.929
We don't know.

00:24:34.005 --> 00:24:35.529
He went away for a minute.

00:24:35.607 --> 00:24:37.040
He screamed,
and we found him here.

00:24:37.108 --> 00:24:38.405
These look like chemical burns.

00:24:38.477 --> 00:24:41.446
Without tricorders,
it's hard to make a diagnosis.

00:24:41.513 --> 00:24:43.071
It's here.

00:24:43.148 --> 00:24:44.672
What?

00:24:44.749 --> 00:24:46.182
The creature.

00:24:46.251 --> 00:24:48.185
You're hallucinating.

00:24:48.253 --> 00:24:51.620
It's the radiation, but you're
going to be all right.

00:24:51.690 --> 00:24:53.624
No!

00:24:53.692 --> 00:24:56.058
It attacked me.

00:24:56.127 --> 00:24:58.527
It... a...

00:24:59.631 --> 00:25:01.462
He's going into shock...
cortical stimulator.

00:25:01.533 --> 00:25:02.932
Pelk, get up!

00:25:07.506 --> 00:25:09.599
He's not responding.

00:25:22.687 --> 00:25:24.450
He said the creature
attacked him.

00:25:24.523 --> 00:25:26.457
He imagined it.

00:25:26.525 --> 00:25:29.619
He was probably scalded
when that conduit ruptured.

00:25:29.694 --> 00:25:32.288
Or maybe there is someone else
on this ship.

00:25:33.498 --> 00:25:34.795
Voyager to away team.

00:25:34.866 --> 00:25:36.458
Transporter interference
has cleared.

00:25:36.535 --> 00:25:38.264
We're locked on
to your coordinates. Standby.

00:25:38.336 --> 00:25:40.930
Harry... Pelk is dead.

00:25:41.072 --> 00:25:42.903
Lock onto his signal
and beam him to Sick Bay.

00:25:42.974 --> 00:25:46.171
Ask the Doctor to determine
the cause of death.

00:25:46.244 --> 00:25:46.972
Aye, sir.

00:25:50.081 --> 00:25:51.343
Someone still needs

00:25:51.416 --> 00:25:53.247
to get up there
and open the air locks.

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:54.751
Me.

00:25:54.819 --> 00:25:56.184
Hold on.

00:25:56.254 --> 00:25:58.188
I'll join you.

00:25:58.256 --> 00:26:00.656
From now on, nobody works alone.

00:26:12.103 --> 00:26:14.003
Progress?

00:26:14.072 --> 00:26:16.267
They've vented five decks...
ten to go.

00:26:16.341 --> 00:26:18.002
At this rate,

00:26:18.076 --> 00:26:20.670
they'll reach the control room
in approximately three hours.

00:26:20.745 --> 00:26:23.305
However, the storage tanks
will detonate in less than two.

00:26:23.381 --> 00:26:25.747
I've been working
on a contingency plan.

00:26:25.817 --> 00:26:27.307
An O-type star.

00:26:27.385 --> 00:26:30.286
If the freighter exploded
within the star's corona,

00:26:30.355 --> 00:26:32.016
it might absorb the radiation.

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:34.718
The star is not
in the freighter's trajectory.

00:26:34.793 --> 00:26:37.626
What if we gave it
a little nudge?

00:26:37.696 --> 00:26:40.221
A series of carefully timed
tractor pulses

00:26:40.298 --> 00:26:42.391
could alter
the freighter's course,

00:26:42.467 --> 00:26:44.128
but, given the vessel's
weakened state,

00:26:44.202 --> 00:26:46.466
one miscalculation
could set off the explosions.

00:26:46.538 --> 00:26:48.733
I'm still counting on
the away team to succeed.

00:26:48.807 --> 00:26:51.776
But I want to be ready with
Plan B if they don't.

00:26:54.412 --> 00:26:56.573
I don't know
about the rest of you,

00:26:56.648 --> 00:26:58.616
but I could sure use
a sonic shower.

00:26:58.683 --> 00:27:01.481
I'd love to soak
in a hot bath for a day or two.

00:27:01.553 --> 00:27:03.714
Oh, not me... I want to feel
those sonic pulses

00:27:03.788 --> 00:27:06.450
dissolving every last atom
of this grime off my body.

00:27:06.524 --> 00:27:09.357
We have
a decontamination bay on board

00:27:09.427 --> 00:27:11.691
that can purge
up to 50 workers at a time.

00:27:11.763 --> 00:27:13.458
Well, that sounds like fun.

00:27:18.870 --> 00:27:21.031
B'Elanna?

00:27:21.106 --> 00:27:23.336
I'm okay.
I'm just a little light-headed.

00:27:25.143 --> 00:27:27.077
Your hand.

00:27:27.145 --> 00:27:29.010
Oh, God...

00:27:31.182 --> 00:27:32.444
Freighter blight...

00:27:32.517 --> 00:27:34.075
from the prolonged exposure.

00:27:34.152 --> 00:27:35.278
Lovely.

00:27:35.353 --> 00:27:38.686
In my business,
it's an occupational hazard.

00:27:38.757 --> 00:27:40.158
We'd better try inoculating
you again.

00:27:40.225 --> 00:27:41.385
If she's blistering,

00:27:41.459 --> 00:27:43.586
she's already received
a fatal dose of radiation.

00:27:43.662 --> 00:27:44.686
She needs treatment.

00:27:44.763 --> 00:27:46.060
I'll live.
Let's keep moving.

00:27:46.131 --> 00:27:47.621
We have medicines
in the infirmary.

00:27:47.699 --> 00:27:49.132
It's only two sections
from here.

00:27:49.200 --> 00:27:51.293
We don't have time for a detour.

00:27:51.369 --> 00:27:52.563
B'Elanna, go with him.

00:27:52.637 --> 00:27:54.366
We'll meet you outside
the control room.

00:27:54.439 --> 00:27:55.804
Chakotay, I'm fine.

00:27:55.874 --> 00:27:57.205
I said go.

00:28:11.856 --> 00:28:14.154
This is the infirmary?

00:28:14.225 --> 00:28:16.056
Looks more like a morgue.

00:28:20.331 --> 00:28:22.595
What happened to him?

00:28:22.667 --> 00:28:24.897
It looks like he
was being treated

00:28:25.003 --> 00:28:26.265
for long-term exposure.

00:28:26.337 --> 00:28:29.101
He was probably left behind
during the evacuation.

00:28:29.174 --> 00:28:31.108
Tough luck, huh?

00:28:31.176 --> 00:28:33.406
There was nothing more
we could do for him.

00:28:33.478 --> 00:28:34.911
He was a core laborer.

00:28:35.046 --> 00:28:37.071
Meaning?

00:28:37.148 --> 00:28:39.082
He worked close
to the storage tanks.

00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:42.313
Only three of ten core laborers
survive a standard mission.

00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:45.686
Occupational hazard?

00:28:45.757 --> 00:28:47.918
They know the risks
when they accept the assignment.

00:28:48.059 --> 00:28:50.584
They know they're going
to end up like this?

00:28:50.662 --> 00:28:53.028
Core laborers can make more
in two months

00:28:53.098 --> 00:28:55.123
than most Malon make
in a lifetime.

00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:56.132
What good is the money

00:28:56.201 --> 00:28:57.600
if they're not around
to collect it?

00:28:59.704 --> 00:29:01.672
It will go to his family.

00:29:04.442 --> 00:29:06.603
What is that thing?

00:29:06.678 --> 00:29:08.612
It's a subdermal injector.

00:29:08.680 --> 00:29:12.878
It contains analeptic compounds
to reverse the cell damage.

00:29:12.951 --> 00:29:15.317
I feel better already.

00:29:15.386 --> 00:29:17.854
I won't hurt you.

00:29:17.922 --> 00:29:19.913
I've done this a hundred times.

00:29:23.361 --> 00:29:26.489
You'll feel a slight
burning sensation.

00:29:29.901 --> 00:29:31.766
Commander...

00:29:31.836 --> 00:29:33.770
the Captain's Plan B.

00:29:33.838 --> 00:29:35.669
I've calculated
the inertial force

00:29:35.740 --> 00:29:37.571
required to divert
the freighter.

00:29:37.642 --> 00:29:40.304
Plan C: Shield modulations
that should reduce

00:29:40.378 --> 00:29:42.243
the structural damage
of Voyager.

00:29:42.313 --> 00:29:44.213
It will also help
protect the crew

00:29:44.282 --> 00:29:47.046
against theta radiation
poisoning... if we fail.

00:29:47.118 --> 00:29:49.086
A wise precaution.

00:29:49.154 --> 00:29:51.122
With any luck,
we won't be needing it.

00:29:51.189 --> 00:29:53.589
I didn't think
Vulcans believed in luck.

00:29:53.658 --> 00:29:55.148
As a rule, we don't,

00:29:55.226 --> 00:29:58.559
but serving with Captain Janeway
has taught me otherwise.

00:29:58.630 --> 00:30:00.461
She does seem to succeed

00:30:00.532 --> 00:30:02.864
more often than random chance
would allow.

00:30:02.934 --> 00:30:04.799
I'll factor it
into my calculations.

00:30:06.571 --> 00:30:09.768
Is there a Plan D?

00:30:09.841 --> 00:30:11.809
No.

00:30:17.248 --> 00:30:19.443
Initiating decompression
sequence, Deck 4!

00:30:19.517 --> 00:30:20.950
Deck clear!

00:30:21.019 --> 00:30:22.714
12 Down! Three to go!

00:30:28.293 --> 00:30:30.761
The air locks are opening
on this deck!

00:30:30.829 --> 00:30:32.626
What?!

00:30:32.697 --> 00:30:33.925
I can't close them!

00:30:33.998 --> 00:30:36.125
Force fields!
Where are they?

00:30:36.201 --> 00:30:37.668
They're off-line!

00:30:37.735 --> 00:30:39.066
We've got to get off this deck!

00:30:39.137 --> 00:30:40.934
Move!

00:30:41.005 --> 00:30:43.303
This way!

00:31:04.229 --> 00:31:05.856
Chakotay!

00:31:05.930 --> 00:31:07.329
He was right behind me.

00:31:07.398 --> 00:31:08.956
Torres to Chakotay.

00:31:10.735 --> 00:31:12.760
That deck is a vacuum by now.

00:31:12.837 --> 00:31:13.929
Torres to Voyager.

00:31:14.005 --> 00:31:14.937
Acknowledged.

00:31:15.039 --> 00:31:16.700
Lock on
to Chakotay's com signal

00:31:16.774 --> 00:31:18.139
and beam him to Sick Bay.

00:31:21.846 --> 00:31:24.371
We've got him.

00:31:24.449 --> 00:31:26.440
He's okay.

00:31:26.517 --> 00:31:28.417
I thought that deck was secure!

00:31:28.486 --> 00:31:29.612
It was.

00:31:29.687 --> 00:31:31.678
Then why did we almost
get blown into space?

00:31:31.756 --> 00:31:33.690
I don't know.

00:31:33.758 --> 00:31:35.191
Air locks don't open
by themselves!

00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:36.522
What are you saying?

00:31:36.594 --> 00:31:37.925
You think it was me?

00:31:37.996 --> 00:31:39.463
Calm down, both of you!

00:31:39.530 --> 00:31:41.964
We don't have time to argue
about what happened.

00:31:42.033 --> 00:31:43.933
We've got to keep moving.

00:31:59.684 --> 00:32:00.810
Chakotay?

00:32:00.885 --> 00:32:02.477
Unconscious but stable.

00:32:02.553 --> 00:32:04.180
The Doctor is treating him now.

00:32:04.255 --> 00:32:06.189
We'll be able to talk to him
in less than an hour.

00:32:06.257 --> 00:32:07.519
I'll want a full report.

00:32:07.592 --> 00:32:08.820
Shall I beam to the freighter

00:32:08.893 --> 00:32:10.383
and take command
of the away team?

00:32:10.461 --> 00:32:11.393
I just spoke with B'Elanna.

00:32:11.462 --> 00:32:12.724
She's got everything
under control.

00:32:12.797 --> 00:32:15.357
This is a dangerous situation.

00:32:15.433 --> 00:32:17.765
There is no margin
for emotional error.

00:32:17.835 --> 00:32:19.097
We have plenty to do here.

00:32:19.170 --> 00:32:21.001
Help me remodulate
the tractor beam.

00:32:23.041 --> 00:32:25.134
B'Elanna is unpredictable,
Captain.

00:32:25.209 --> 00:32:26.233
Under these circumstances,

00:32:26.311 --> 00:32:28.779
her volatile nature could
compromise the mission.

00:32:28.846 --> 00:32:31.747
Your concerns are noted,
but, if I send you over there,

00:32:31.816 --> 00:32:33.249
I'd be sending
the wrong message...

00:32:33.318 --> 00:32:35.377
that I don't have faith
in her, but I do.

00:32:35.453 --> 00:32:37.944
Your faith is admirable,
but logic suggests...

00:32:38.022 --> 00:32:39.353
This isn't about logic.

00:32:39.424 --> 00:32:40.413
It's about trust.

00:32:40.491 --> 00:32:41.924
She'll come through for us.

00:32:41.993 --> 00:32:43.255
Now, give me a hand.

00:32:46.264 --> 00:32:47.822
Lieutenant?

00:32:52.370 --> 00:32:53.394
Lieute...

00:32:54.839 --> 00:32:56.101
Are you all right?

00:32:56.174 --> 00:32:58.074
Fine.

00:32:58.142 --> 00:32:59.336
Report.

00:32:59.410 --> 00:33:00.809
We just vented the last deck.

00:33:00.878 --> 00:33:03.244
We should have a clear path
to the control room.

00:33:04.716 --> 00:33:07.082
Let's get this thing
over with then.

00:33:07.151 --> 00:33:08.812
If you need to rest...

00:33:08.886 --> 00:33:10.183
I said I'm fine.

00:33:14.359 --> 00:33:15.917
I was...

00:33:15.994 --> 00:33:17.256
meditating.

00:33:17.328 --> 00:33:19.319
Meditating?

00:33:20.665 --> 00:33:21.962
You?

00:33:24.068 --> 00:33:25.365
Do me a favor.

00:33:25.436 --> 00:33:27.199
Don't tell Tuvok.

00:33:27.271 --> 00:33:30.729
Your secret's safe.

00:33:30.808 --> 00:33:33.072
It's this place.

00:33:33.144 --> 00:33:34.611
I know how you feel.

00:33:34.679 --> 00:33:37.648
The next time I volunteer
to board

00:33:37.715 --> 00:33:40.115
a Malon freighter,
check me into Sick Bay

00:33:40.184 --> 00:33:41.947
and have my head examined.

00:33:42.086 --> 00:33:44.054
I feel like
I'm ready to explode.

00:33:44.122 --> 00:33:46.955
We'll get through this together.

00:33:47.025 --> 00:33:50.392
I got a knack for diffusing
explosive situations.

00:33:51.963 --> 00:33:53.157
Thanks.

00:33:57.668 --> 00:34:00.034
Aw...

00:34:01.105 --> 00:34:02.402
Torres to Astrometrics.

00:34:02.473 --> 00:34:03.599
Go ahead.

00:34:03.674 --> 00:34:04.834
We're outside the control room,

00:34:04.909 --> 00:34:05.841
but without tricorders,

00:34:05.910 --> 00:34:07.502
we can't tell
if it's safe to go in there.

00:34:08.646 --> 00:34:10.113
The room is too heavily
shielded.

00:34:10.181 --> 00:34:11.648
Our sensors can't penetrate it.

00:34:11.716 --> 00:34:13.206
You must stand by.

00:34:13.284 --> 00:34:15.411
The theta dampening field
is still active.

00:34:15.486 --> 00:34:16.510
It should be safe.

00:34:18.790 --> 00:34:19.814
After you.

00:34:31.803 --> 00:34:33.668
It's worse than I expected.

00:34:33.738 --> 00:34:37.401
Theta gas has leaked
into the warp manifold.

00:34:37.475 --> 00:34:40.569
We've got less than ten minutes
before this vessel explodes!

00:34:40.645 --> 00:34:42.579
Emergency systems are down.

00:34:43.714 --> 00:34:45.944
This should feed enough energy
to your power matrix

00:34:46.017 --> 00:34:47.644
to reinitialize them.

00:34:47.718 --> 00:34:49.345
Try it now.

00:34:52.523 --> 00:34:54.548
They're coming back on line,

00:34:54.625 --> 00:34:57.594
but only one containment grid
is still operational.

00:34:57.662 --> 00:34:58.890
We have two unstable tanks.

00:34:58.963 --> 00:35:00.453
One grid can't handle them both.

00:35:00.531 --> 00:35:03.022
We'll seal them one at a time.

00:35:05.670 --> 00:35:06.967
Doctor?

00:35:08.272 --> 00:35:09.239
Easy, Commander.

00:35:09.307 --> 00:35:10.706
Ow, my head aches.

00:35:10.775 --> 00:35:12.208
I'm not surprised.

00:35:12.276 --> 00:35:13.800
You took a severe blow.

00:35:13.878 --> 00:35:15.812
I've got to get back
to the freighter.

00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:17.313
Not in this condition.

00:35:17.381 --> 00:35:18.780
If you want to help,

00:35:18.850 --> 00:35:21.910
you can answer some questions
about Mr. Pelk's death.

00:35:22.053 --> 00:35:25.545
I've found unidentified
tissue in his wounds.

00:35:25.623 --> 00:35:27.113
What sort of tissue?

00:35:27.191 --> 00:35:29.625
The computer is running
a microcellular scan.

00:35:29.694 --> 00:35:32.219
Pelk said he was attacked.

00:35:32.296 --> 00:35:35.356
Ah, yes, the Malon bogeyman.

00:35:35.433 --> 00:35:38.334
Microcellular analysis
is complete.

00:35:44.142 --> 00:35:49.170
Odd. The tissue is saturated
with theta radiation,

00:35:49.247 --> 00:35:52.614
but it's not showing signs
of decay.

00:35:52.683 --> 00:35:55.208
It came from someone...
or something...

00:35:55.286 --> 00:35:58.380
that's developed
a resistance to the radiation.

00:35:58.456 --> 00:36:00.287
Sick Bay to Seven of Nine.

00:36:00.358 --> 00:36:01.655
Yes, Doctor.

00:36:01.726 --> 00:36:04.126
Scan for additional life-forms
aboard the Malon vessel.

00:36:04.195 --> 00:36:05.685
I've been running
continuous scans.

00:36:05.763 --> 00:36:08.493
I assure you there is no one
there aside from the away team.

00:36:08.566 --> 00:36:10.363
This life-form's
heavily irradiated.

00:36:10.434 --> 00:36:12.766
It could be blending in
with ambient toxins.

00:36:12.837 --> 00:36:15.533
I'll recalibrate our sensors.

00:36:16.874 --> 00:36:18.501
Tank 1 stable.

00:36:18.576 --> 00:36:21.409
Reroute the containment grid
to Tank 2.

00:36:21.479 --> 00:36:23.913
What happened?

00:36:23.981 --> 00:36:25.642
A power surge!

00:36:25.716 --> 00:36:27.149
We're losing the grid.

00:36:27.218 --> 00:36:29.914
It was triggered
from a workstation on this deck.

00:36:30.054 --> 00:36:31.351
Janeway to away team.

00:36:31.422 --> 00:36:34.016
We've detected an alien
life-form aboard the freighter.

00:36:34.091 --> 00:36:35.319
We believe it killed Pelk.

00:36:35.393 --> 00:36:37.156
Captain, we just lost power.

00:36:37.228 --> 00:36:39.560
We're diverting the freighter
into a nearby star.

00:36:39.630 --> 00:36:41.928
Leave the control room
so we can get a lock on you.

00:36:41.999 --> 00:36:43.193
Acknowledged.

00:36:47.038 --> 00:36:48.300
What's going on?

00:36:48.372 --> 00:36:49.669
It's jammed!

00:36:49.740 --> 00:36:53.301
Seven of Nine to away team.
I've detected

00:36:53.377 --> 00:36:54.639
the alien life-form.

00:36:54.712 --> 00:36:56.976
It's moving
toward your position.

00:37:04.689 --> 00:37:07.658
The gas is being routed through
the environmental system!

00:37:07.725 --> 00:37:09.886
I'll try to shut it down!

00:37:09.994 --> 00:37:11.757
Is there another way out?

00:37:11.829 --> 00:37:13.456
No.

00:37:14.599 --> 00:37:15.759
Do you have them?

00:37:15.833 --> 00:37:17.767
Not yet.

00:37:21.439 --> 00:37:23.669
The life-form has entered
the control room.

00:37:38.256 --> 00:37:39.746
I'm trying to vent the gas,

00:37:39.824 --> 00:37:41.587
but the release valves
are jammed.

00:37:41.659 --> 00:37:44.150
Use the environmental controls
instead.

00:37:44.228 --> 00:37:47.163
In the meantime, see if you
can get that hatch open.

00:37:51.736 --> 00:37:52.725
Neelix?

00:37:56.007 --> 00:37:57.599
No, you'll ignite the gas.

00:38:03.447 --> 00:38:04.607
Neelix?

00:38:13.658 --> 00:38:16.252
We've got to get him back
to Voyager.

00:38:16.327 --> 00:38:17.589
Get that hatch open!

00:38:17.662 --> 00:38:20.222
I'm trying!

00:38:22.199 --> 00:38:23.757
Fesek, behind you!

00:39:13.751 --> 00:39:15.878
You're a core laborer.

00:39:15.953 --> 00:39:17.818
Not anymore.

00:39:19.890 --> 00:39:21.289
Stay back.

00:39:24.428 --> 00:39:25.861
Don't make me kill you.

00:39:27.398 --> 00:39:30.265
I'm already dead.

00:39:37.108 --> 00:39:39.838
You've been
sabotaging this ship.

00:39:39.910 --> 00:39:43.141
There's no other way
to make them understand.

00:39:43.214 --> 00:39:46.911
So that's your way of getting
even... killing your crew?

00:39:46.984 --> 00:39:50.147
Causing an explosion that
will contaminate other ships?

00:39:50.221 --> 00:39:52.655
They poisoned me!

00:40:03.501 --> 00:40:05.594
The freighter's on course
for the star.

00:40:05.669 --> 00:40:07.933
Away team, we've adjusted
the vessel's course.

00:40:08.038 --> 00:40:09.699
It's heading for an O-type star.

00:40:09.774 --> 00:40:11.366
You have to get out of there
now.

00:40:11.442 --> 00:40:12.932
No.

00:40:13.077 --> 00:40:15.204
No!

00:40:20.951 --> 00:40:24.546
The freighter's maneuvering
thrusters just activated.

00:40:24.622 --> 00:40:25.782
It's altering course.

00:40:25.856 --> 00:40:27.016
Compensate.

00:40:29.260 --> 00:40:30.284
No effect.

00:40:30.361 --> 00:40:32.420
I'm detecting radiation surges
in the theta tanks.

00:40:32.496 --> 00:40:33.963
They're going to detonate
in three minutes.

00:40:34.031 --> 00:40:35.157
Harry?

00:40:35.232 --> 00:40:37.325
As long as they're
in the control room,

00:40:37.401 --> 00:40:38.663
I can't get a lock.

00:40:38.736 --> 00:40:40.465
Janeway to away team.
Get those maneuvering

00:40:40.538 --> 00:40:41.766
thruster off-line.

00:40:41.839 --> 00:40:43.670
Then get
out of the contaminated area.

00:40:43.741 --> 00:40:45.868
We can't get
a transporter lock on you.

00:40:45.943 --> 00:40:48.969
Get the hell away
from there, now!

00:40:49.046 --> 00:40:50.570
No!

00:40:50.648 --> 00:40:52.343
It's too late!

00:40:55.085 --> 00:40:58.418
Okay. Okay.

00:41:00.558 --> 00:41:01.889
Look...

00:41:01.959 --> 00:41:03.927
I know what they've done to you.

00:41:04.061 --> 00:41:05.358
They used you.

00:41:05.429 --> 00:41:07.556
You want to hurt them.
Listen.

00:41:07.631 --> 00:41:08.859
Listen to me.

00:41:08.933 --> 00:41:10.901
I know...
I know that you're so angry,

00:41:10.968 --> 00:41:13.732
you want to destroy everything
in sight, but there's

00:41:13.804 --> 00:41:15.931
another way to make
them understand.

00:41:16.040 --> 00:41:17.507
I'm on your side.

00:41:17.575 --> 00:41:19.406
I can help you.

00:41:21.345 --> 00:41:25.543
Innocent people are going to die
if you do this.

00:41:27.351 --> 00:41:30.445
No. It's over.

00:41:30.521 --> 00:41:32.614
Please. Please.

00:41:33.824 --> 00:41:35.416
Please, let me help you.

00:41:35.493 --> 00:41:36.721
No.

00:41:39.663 --> 00:41:42.063
Step away!

00:41:53.344 --> 00:41:55.312
The Malon's thrusters
are powering down.

00:41:56.380 --> 00:41:58.644
I've restored
the freighter's trajectory.

00:41:59.717 --> 00:42:01.480
B'Elanna, get out of there.

00:42:01.552 --> 00:42:04.146
Come on, we've got to go.

00:42:11.462 --> 00:42:12.520
Fesek...

00:42:38.689 --> 00:42:39.747
The away team, Mr. Kim.

00:42:39.823 --> 00:42:41.757
I got them.

00:42:51.368 --> 00:42:54.929
Maybe the meditation's working.

00:42:55.005 --> 00:42:57.337
What makes you say that?

00:42:57.408 --> 00:42:59.342
From what Neelix told me,

00:42:59.410 --> 00:43:01.742
you kept your temper
in check over there.

00:43:03.981 --> 00:43:06.313
Don't expect me
to make a habit of it.

00:43:06.383 --> 00:43:08.214
Well, I've repaired

00:43:08.285 --> 00:43:10.913
most of your cellular
degradation.

00:43:11.055 --> 00:43:13.353
I wish I could say
the same for you,

00:43:13.424 --> 00:43:16.222
but you've suffered
long-term systemic damage.

00:43:16.293 --> 00:43:19.421
Your condition will
deteriorate over time.

00:43:19.496 --> 00:43:21.623
It's an occupational hazard.

00:43:21.699 --> 00:43:23.929
We've contacted
a Malon transport ship

00:43:24.034 --> 00:43:25.467
in the next sector.

00:43:25.536 --> 00:43:28.027
We've altered course
to rendezvous with them.

00:43:28.105 --> 00:43:30.300
Thank you, Captain.

00:43:30.374 --> 00:43:33.639
I don't know how I'm going
to explain what happened.

00:43:33.711 --> 00:43:35.042
Tell them the truth.

00:43:36.914 --> 00:43:39.348
Tell them
the vihaar is no myth.

00:44:42.846 --> 00:44:45.406
Computer, activate sonic shower.
